Coordinator request ownership fix for bundled librdkafka 2.16.0.
Based on https://github.com/confluentinc/librdkafka/pull/5397 (unmerged).
Keep the worker alive until the error response consumes its eonce reference.
Do not enqueue a response if the admin operation has already been destroyed.
The upstream proposal's generic NULL-opaque guard is intentionally omitted:
NULL can be valid callback data for non-admin coordinator requests.

--- a/src/rdkafka_admin.c
+++ b/src/rdkafka_admin.c
@@ -485,1 +485,0 @@
-        rd_kafka_t *rk             = rkb->rkb_rk;
@@ -504,7 +503,3 @@
-        if (err) {
-                rd_kafka_admin_result_fail(
-                    rko, err, "%s worker failed to send request: %s",
-                    rd_kafka_op2str(rko->rko_type), errstr);
-                rd_kafka_admin_common_worker_destroy(rk, rko,
-                                                     rd_true /*destroy*/);
-        }
+        /* The coordinator caller delivers errors through the response callback,
+         * which owns destruction of rko and its eonce. Destroying them here
+         * would leave the queued error response with a freed opaque pointer. */
--- a/src/rdkafka_coord.c
+++ b/src/rdkafka_coord.c
@@ -506,1 +506,7 @@
-                        if (err) {
+                        if (err == RD_KAFKA_RESP_ERR__DESTROY) {
+                                /* The admin operation has timed out and released
+                                 * its opaque. Do not enqueue another response. */
+                                rd_kafka_replyq_destroy(&replyq);
+                                rd_kafka_coord_req_destroy(rk, creq,
+                                                           rd_true /*done*/);
+                        } else if (err) {
